  "about": "A small line drawing of a landmark or a view for a city, for the stamps on the Year page. A key is the city's name as data.js writes it, a comma and the ISO-3166 alpha-2 country code. `d` is an SVG path in a box 100 wide and 70 high, drawn as a stroke only, with the ground near y = 60; `name` and `zh` say what it shows. A country reached for the first time whose first city is not listed here keeps the outline of the country as its stamp. The drawings were made by hand and are simplified; most were checked against photographs on Wikimedia Commons (not the Stone Bridge, and Hagere Maryam shows a general highland view); corrections and new cities are welcome.",
